{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"proxy-reflect","title":"Proxy & Reflect","group":"Advanced Concepts","order":52,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">A <code>Proxy</code> wraps an object and intercepts fundamental operations — get, set, delete, <code>in</code>, function calls. <code>Reflect</code> provides the default behaviour for each trap.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list\"></i>Traps</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Trap</th><th>Intercepts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>get(target, prop, receiver)</code></td><td><code>obj.prop</code>, <code>obj[prop]</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>set(target, prop, value, receiver)</code></td><td><code>obj.prop = value</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>has(target, prop)</code></td><td><code>prop in obj</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>deleteProperty(target, prop)</code></td><td><code>delete obj.prop</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>ownKeys(target)</code></td><td><code>Object.keys</code>, <code>for…in</code>, <code>Reflect.ownKeys</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>apply(target, thisArg, args)</code></td><td>Calling a function proxy</td></tr><tr><td><code>construct(target, args)</code></td><td><code>new</code> on a proxy</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-shield-check\"></i>Validation and defaults</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const user = new Proxy({}, {\n  set(target, prop, value, receiver) {\n    if (prop === \"age\" &amp;&amp; (!Number.isInteger(value) || value &lt; 0)) {\n      throw new TypeError(`age must be a non-negative integer, got ${value}`);\n    }\n    return Reflect.set(target, prop, value, receiver);   // default behaviour\n  },\n  get(target, prop, receiver) {\n    return prop in target ? Reflect.get(target, prop, receiver) : `&lt;no ${String(prop)}&gt;`;\n  },\n});\nuser.name = \"Asha\";\nuser.age = 30;\ntry { user.age = -5; } catch (e) { console.log(e.message); }\nconsole.log(user.name, user.age, user.email);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>age must be a non-negative integer, got -5\nAsha 30 &lt;no email&gt;</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-eye\"></i>Observing changes (how Vue 3 reactivity works)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function reactive(obj, onChange) {\n  return new Proxy(obj, {\n    set(target, prop, value) {\n      const old = target[prop];\n      const ok = Reflect.set(target, prop, value);\n      if (old !== value) onChange(prop, old, value);\n      return ok;\n    },\n  });\n}\nconst state = reactive({ count: 0 }, (k, a, b) =&gt; console.log(`${k}: ${a} → ${b}`));\nstate.count++;\nstate.count += 5;\nstate.count = 6;          // unchanged → no notification</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>count: 0 → 1\ncount: 1 → 6</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-eye-off\"></i>Negative array indices, and hiding private keys</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const arr = new Proxy([10, 20, 30], {\n  get(target, prop, receiver) {\n    const i = Number(prop);\n    return Number.isInteger(i) &amp;&amp; i &lt; 0 ? target[target.length + i] : Reflect.get(target, prop, receiver);\n  },\n});\nconsole.log(arr[-1], arr[0], arr.length);\n\nconst hidden = new Proxy({ id: 1, _secret: \"x\" }, {\n  has: (t, p) =&gt; !String(p).startsWith(\"_\") &amp;&amp; p in t,\n  ownKeys: (t) =&gt; Reflect.ownKeys(t).filter((k) =&gt; !String(k).startsWith(\"_\")),\n});\nconsole.log(\"_secret\" in hidden, Object.keys(hidden));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>30 10 3\nfalse [ 'id' ]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-left-right\"></i>Reflect</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const obj = { a: 1 };\nconsole.log(Reflect.has(obj, \"a\"), Reflect.ownKeys(obj), Reflect.get(obj, \"a\"));\nconsole.log(Reflect.defineProperty(Object.freeze({}), \"x\", { value: 1 }));   // false, no throw\nconsole.log(Reflect.apply(Math.max, null, [1, 5, 3]));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>true [ 'a' ] 1\nfalse\n5</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p><code>Reflect</code> methods mirror the proxy traps one-to-one and return booleans instead of throwing. Inside a trap, forward to <code>Reflect.x(...)</code> with the same arguments (including <code>receiver</code>) to keep getters and inheritance working.</p></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>Proxies add overhead to every intercepted operation, and <code>===</code> sees the proxy and target as different objects. Built-ins with internal slots (<code>Map</code>, <code>Date</code>, <code>#private</code> fields) don't work transparently through a proxy.</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What are real-world uses of Proxy?</summary><div><p>Reactivity systems (Vue 3, MobX), validation, default values, logging/tracing, access control, negative indexing, API clients that turn property access into requests, and mocks in tests.</p></div></details></section>"}